# {{name}}

{{summary}} Built on [operonx](https://pypi.org/project/operonx/).

`src/greeting/` is the feature: `ops.py` holds the logic, `graph.py` wires
it. `app/main.py` declares what runs it: the `greet_people` job over
`datasets/people.jsonl`, and the `greet` HTTP service.

## Run

```bash
uv sync
uv run pytest                     # the tests, offline
uv run operonx run greet_people   # greet everyone in datasets/people.jsonl → out/greetings.jsonl
```

## Serve

```bash
uv run operonx serve --list       # what would listen, and where
uv run operonx serve              # POST /greet on :8000 (PORT overrides)
curl -s localhost:8000/greet -d '{"id": "x", "name": "grace"}'
```

## Grow it

A new feature is a new folder under `src/` with its own `graph.py` and
`ops.py`, and one more entry in `app/main.py`. Read `AGENTS.md` and
`.operonx/guide/README.md` first.
